title: The Knives Come Out
subtitle: The bureaucrats are preparing to move against us.
tags: event
view-if: bureau_relation <= 10 and (rc_in_govt or rc_chairs > 0) and not bureau_warn_hostile and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 3
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_chancellery.svg
on-arrival: bureau_warn_hostile = 1

= The Knives Come Out

A friendly committee secretary warns us over caf: files about the Caucus are being assembled, leaks are being prepared, and the Vice Chair's office has been asking which of our partners could be persuaded to govern without us.

The Senate bureaucracy is now **hostile**. [? if rc_chancellor : If relations fall any further, they will manufacture a crisis around our Chancellor and push the Senate towards a vote of no confidence, as they did to Valorum. ?][? if not rc_chancellor : If relations fall any further, they will "reorganise" the committees and force the Caucus out of government. ?]

- @truce: Offer the guilds a truce.
- @valorum_way: Make the bureaucrats an offer they understand.
- @brace: Brace for it.

@truce
subtitle: The guilds and their clerks relax; the Rimward wing is furious.
on-arrival: guild_relation += 8; bureau_relation += 8; rimward_dissent += 5; guild_embargo -= 1

The Caucus quietly drops two bills the guilds dislike. Their lobbyists call off the clerks, for now.

@valorum_way
subtitle: −2 political capital; buys time.
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 2; bureau_relation += 14; corruption += 0.5

Promotions, postings, a new wing for the Senate Archives. It is exactly the kind of deal the Caucus came to the Senate to end.

@brace

The Caucus prepares for the worst and keeps working.
